{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015ima7DXiAwDS15URh6b7j1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I found R4.9 in the file. Here's the complete requirement and its surrounding context:\n\n## R4.9 Requirement\n\n**Text:**\n\"-i, -s, and -F may all be combined with -R. Each subdirectory listing applies the same metadata display and classification options.\"\n\n**Location:** Lines 192-193 in the R4 section\n\n## R4 Section Context\n\n**R4 Title:** \"Exit codes, signal handling, and flag interactions\"\n\nR4 is the section dealing with how the `ls` command handles:\n- Exit codes (R4.1-R4.3): Exiting 0 on success, 1 on minor problems, 2 on serious problems\n- Signal handling (R4.4-R4.5): SIGPIPE and SIGWINCH handlers\n- Flag interactions (R4.6-R4.9): How various flags work together\n\n## Complete R4 Requirements (for context)\n\n- **R4.1:** Exit 0 when all paths accessed and output written successfully\n- **R4.2:** Exit 1 on minor problems (access denied, file not found)\n- **R4.3:** Exit 2 on serious problems (invalid command-line option)\n- **R4.4:** Install SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n- **R4.5:** Install SIGWINCH handler via `pkg/sys.OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))`\n- **R4.6:** -n implies -l (numeric UID/GID in long format)\n- **R4.7:** -C and -x are mutually exclusive with -l and -1; last flag wins\n- **R4.8:** -R with -l must produce \"total N\" block line for each subdirectory\n- **R4.9:** **-i, -s, and -F may all be combined with -R. Each subdirectory listing applies the same metadata display and classification options.**\n\n## Related Non-Goals\n\nThe specification notes these are out of scope (relevant to recursive operations):\n- --hyperlink (terminal hyperlinks)\n- --dired (Emacs dired mode)\n- -Z (SELinux security context)\n- --quoting-style (filename quoting)\n- --block-size=SIZE with arbitrary unit suffixes\n- LS_COLORS environment variable parsing\n- ACL (access control list) display\n- --group-directories-first\n- -w / --width (explicit width override)\n- --sort=WORD (long-form sort option)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Tracing R4.9\n\nR4.9 is traced by these acceptance criteria:\n- **AC13:** Inode display with -R\n- **AC14:** Block count display with -R\n- **AC16:** Classify (-F) with -R\n- **AC17:** Full recursive listing test combining all recursive options"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4f33632-7054-4942-b764-2cf5fa4c4252","uuid":"3abf90d3-595e-4f07-a411-6e6a649a16bf","timestamp":"2026-05-14T23:06:01.751Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read the file docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml and find requirement R4.9. I need to know exactly what R4.9 specifies - the full requirement text, acceptance criteria, and any related context. Report the complete R4.9 requirement and its surrounding context (what R4 group is about, any non_goals that might be relevant).","agentId":"a4382a33765c4d77e","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I found R4.9 in the file. Here's the complete requirement and its surrounding context:\n\n## R4.9 Requirement\n\n**Text:**\n\"-i, -s, and -F may all be combined with -R. Each subdirectory listing applies the same metadata display and classification options.\"\n\n**Location:** Lines 192-193 in the R4 section\n\n## R4 Section Context\n\n**R4 Title:** \"Exit codes, signal handling, and flag interactions\"\n\nR4 is the section dealing with how the `ls` command handles:\n- Exit codes (R4.1-R4.3): Exiting 0 on success, 1 on minor problems, 2 on serious problems\n- Signal handling (R4.4-R4.5): SIGPIPE and SIGWINCH handlers\n- Flag interactions (R4.6-R4.9): How various flags work together\n\n## Complete R4 Requirements (for context)\n\n- **R4.1:** Exit 0 when all paths accessed and output written successfully\n- **R4.2:** Exit 1 on minor problems (access denied, file not found)\n- **R4.3:** Exit 2 on serious problems (invalid command-line option)\n- **R4.4:** Install SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n- **R4.5:** Install SIGWINCH handler via `pkg/sys.OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))`\n- **R4.6:** -n implies -l (numeric UID/GID in long format)\n- **R4.7:** -C and -x are mutually exclusive with -l and -1; last flag wins\n- **R4.8:** -R with -l must produce \"total N\" block line for each subdirectory\n- **R4.9:** **-i, -s, and -F may all be combined with -R. Each subdirectory listing applies the same metadata display and classification options.**\n\n## Related Non-Goals\n\nThe specification notes these are out of scope (relevant to recursive operations):\n- --hyperlink (terminal hyperlinks)\n- --dired (Emacs dired mode)\n- -Z (SELinux security context)\n- --quoting-style (filename quoting)\n- --block-size=SIZE with arbitrary unit suffixes\n- LS_COLORS environment variable parsing\n- ACL (access control list) display\n- --group-directories-first\n- -w / --width (explicit width override)\n- --sort=WORD (long-form sort option)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Tracing R4.9\n\nR4.9 is traced by these acceptance criteria:\n- **AC13:** Inode display with -R\n- **AC14:** Block count display with -R\n- **AC16:** Classify (-F) with -R\n- **AC17:** Full recursive listing test combining all recursive options"}],"totalDurationMs":10334,"totalTokens":26602,"totalToolUseCount":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9833,"cache_read_input_tokens":16083,"output_tokens":681,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9833},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":681,"cache_read_input_tokens":16083,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9833,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":1,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount"