{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold pipeline task (#5226) to implement srd008-ls requirement R4.9 in the go-unix-utils project. R4.9 specifies: \"-i, -s, and -F may all be combined with -R. Each subdirectory listing applies the same metadata display and classification options.\" The task requires modifying `cmd/ls/main.go` to implement this flag interaction behavior and `cmd/ls/ls_test.go` to add differential tests verifying the behavior matches the `gls` (GNU ls) reference binary.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing**: Tests compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gls`) using `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **R4.9 requirement**: Flags `-i` (inode), `-s` (block size), and `-F` (classify) must work correctly when combined with `-R` (recursive). Each subdirectory listing must apply the same metadata/classification options.\n   - **Package contracts**: `testutils.DiffTest` struct with fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n   - **pkg/sys**: Provides `Stat`, `Lstat`, `FileInfo`, `TerminalWidth`, `InstallSIGPIPEHandler`\n   - **pkg/format**: Provides `HumanSize`, `FileTypeColor`, `Columns`, `PadRight`, `PadLeft`, `ColorEnabled`\n   - **LC_ALL=C**: All differential tests must set this in the Env field\n   - **SIGPIPE handler**: All cmd/ utilities must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - **Function size limit**: 40 lines max (hard limit from execution constitution)\n   - **File size limit**: 500 lines per Go source file\n   - **No git commands**: Git is managed externally by the orchestrator\n   - **Related acceptance criteria**: AC13 (inode with -R), AC14 (block count with -R), AC16 (classify -F with -R)