ctly when combined with `-R`, with each subdirectory listing applying the same metadata display and classification options\n   - Add differential test cases covering: inode display with -R (AC13), block count display with -R (AC14), classify -F with -R (AC16), and full recursive listing combining all recursive options (AC17)\n   - Run `go build -o bin/ls ./cmd/ls/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/ls/ -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just dispatched an Explore agent to read the SRD requirement R4.9 and received its results. The agent confirmed R4.9 specifies that \"-i, -s, and -F may all be combined with -R. Each subdirectory listing applies the same metadata display and classification options.\" I was about to read the existing `cmd/ls/main.go` and `cmd/ls/ls_test.go` files to understand the current implementation before making changes. No code has been written or modified yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read `cmd/ls/main.go` and `cmd/ls/ls_test.go` to understand the existing implementation, then implement R4.9 by ensuring the recursive listing code (`-R`) properly propagates the `-i` (inode), `-s` (block size), and `-F` (classify) flags to subdirectory listings, and add differential test cases that verify these flag combinations against `gls`. The task description states: \"Implement srd008-ls requirement R4.9 as specified in the SRD\" and the design decision D1 says: \"Extend the existing cmd/ls implementation -- do not restructure or refactor existing code.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5226/a4f33632-7054-4942-b764-2cf5fa4c4252.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not